      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database remains inaccessible (persistent authentication error), so I'll complete the analysis based on the semantic-network evidence and precedent metrics, and construct the SQL accordingly. Below is the full report.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (Phase 1 survivors relevant to the task):**\n\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL** — Extended academic term dimension covering *all* terms known to the warehouse (superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS). Key columns: `TERM_CODE` (YYYYTT), `ACADEMIC_YEAR`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`, `TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR`, `FINANCIAL_AID_YEAR`, `DEGREE_YEAR`. Granularity: one row per academic term. Does **not** carry `IS_REGULAR_TERM`/`TERM_STATUS`.\n- **ACADEMIC_TERMS** — Status-tracked term subset; same calendar attributes plus `IS_REGULAR_TERM`, `TERM_STATUS`, `ADD_DATE`, `DROP_DATE`. Not named in the gold-table hints.\n- **COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year/term: `SUBJECT_ID`, `TERM_CODE`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME` (e.g. 'Mathematics'), unit structure incl. `TOTAL_UNITS`, offering flags, HGN level. Granularity: one row per subject offering per term/academic year.\n- **LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL** — Bridge table linking reserve catalog items, library subject offerings, instructors, and material status per term: `LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY` ('U' = Unknown), `TERM_CODE`, `SUBJECT_ID`, `LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG_KEY`. Granularity: one row per reserve material per subject offering per term.\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — Parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL; subjects in library reserve scope with `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`. Not in gold hints (department filter is anchored to `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME` per the column mapping).\n- **LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS** — Lookup decoding `LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY`: 'U' = Unknown, 'Y' = Required Course Material, etc. Not needed since the question filters on the raw key 'U'.\n\n**Column concepts:**\n\n- **column_concept_total_units** — `TOTAL_UNITS` replicated across catalog/registrar tables; decision guide: \"Unit statistics (avg/stddev/variance) over catalog offerings → use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS.\"\n- **column_concept_material_status_key** — Library vs TIP status keys are independent domains; \"Questions about library reserve material status → filter LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY (e.g. 'U').\"\n- **column_concept_year_columns** — Academic year per term lives in ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL; catalog has its own ACADEMIC_YEAR. Hint maps academic year to `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR`/`ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC`.\n- **column_concept_term_code** — TERM_CODE is the universal join key between term dimension and fact tables.\n- **column_concept_department_name** — \"Filtering subjects by department in catalog analysis → use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\" (plain academic names like 'Mathematics').\n\n**Concepts:** `concept_academic_term_dimension` (ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL = \"source of academic year, academic year description … over the widest term coverage\"); `concept_course_material_programs` (library reserve chain and status semantics); `concept_subject_offering_facts`, `concept_course_catalog_sources`, `concept_department_dimension` (context only).\n\n**Precedent metrics investigated:** `dw_4701` (per-academic-year AVG/STDDEV of TOTAL_UNITS over the population of LRM status-'U' rows joined to terms and COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED **via term code only**), `dw_1301` (Mathematics + ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL + library joins), `dw_3311` (status-'U' library rows with department unit dispersion).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\n- Graph neighbors of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL: joins → ACADEMIC_TERMS, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, LIBRARY_RESERVE_CATALOG, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS, LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR, TIP_DETAIL, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED; concept → concept_course_material_programs; column_concepts → term_code, subject_id, material_status_key.\n- Hint-documented join keys for this task: `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE` and `ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.TERM_CODE ↔ LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.TERM_CODE`. No LRM↔CCSO SUBJECT_ID join key is documented.\n- Precedent `dw_4701` SQL confirms the shape: `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL lrm JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON lrm.TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso ON at.TERM_CODE = ccso.EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE WHERE lrm.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U'` — i.e., reserve materials are combined with catalog TOTAL_UNITS **through the term join**, not through SUBJECT_ID.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (term tables):** ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL = all terms, no status/regular flags (desc + columns); ACADEMIC_TERMS = status-tracked subset with IS_REGULAR_TERM/TERM_STATUS (desc + columns). The question imposes no regular-term/status filter and the hints name ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL → the widest-coverage table is required so every fact-table term resolves to an academic year.\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Academic year + description → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR / ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC: SUPPORTED (hint mapping; columns exist).\n- TOTAL_UNITS measure → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS: SUPPORTED (hint mapping; column exists; decision guide in column_concept_total_units).\n- Mathematics filter → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics': SUPPORTED (hint mapping; column desc gives 'Mathematics' as an example value; precedent dw_1301/dw_104 use exactly this literal).\n- Material status 'U' → LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U': SUPPORTED (hint mapping; column desc lists 'U' = Unknown).\n- Regular-term/status filters: NOT REQUIRED by the question; ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL VIOLATES nothing since no such filter exists.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"academic year description\" → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC (hint). \"total units for subjects offered in terms within that year by the Mathematics department\" → CCSO.TOTAL_UNITS with DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics', terms joined via TERM_CODE (hint join key). \"total units for all library reserve materials with material status 'U' offered in terms by the Mathematics department\" → population = LRM rows with status 'U' in terms, with TOTAL_UNITS taken from CCSO joined through the term (hint lists LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY + CCSO.TOTAL_UNITS as the mapping and only TERM_CODE join keys). \"Coefficient of variation\" = STDDEV(x)/AVG(x), bare STDDEV() per the tips.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** CV/STDDEV-of-TOTAL_UNITS-over-library-'U'-population precedents: dw_4701 (term-code-only join between LRM and CCSO), dw_3311 (department unit dispersion with status 'U'), dw_1301 (Mathematics + ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL + library, though it adds a SUBJECT_ID join for a different measure — enrollment, not TOTAL_UNITS). For the exact task shape (per-year unit statistics over the 'U' reserve population), dw_4701 is the closest precedent and uses the term-level join.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: used as the year/description source in windowed and per-year statistics (concept decision guide; precedents dw_1301, dw_4978, dw_4826).\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: the canonical source for catalog unit statistics per department/year (column_concept_total_units decision guide; many Mathematics-department precedents dw_41, dw_359, dw_1049, dw_1301).\n- LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL: reserve-material counts and status-'U' filtering (table desc; concept_course_material_programs; precedents dw_4701, dw_3311, dw_2850).\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, ACADEMIC_TERMS, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS — semantic_get ✔; LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL — semantic_graph neighbors ✔.\n- column_concept_total_units, column_concept_material_status_key, column_concept_year_columns, column_concept_term_code, column_concept_department_name — semantic_get ✔.\n- concept_academic_term_dimension, concept_course_material_programs — semantic_get ✔.\n- Metrics dw_4701, dw_3311, dw_1301 — semantic_get (full SQL) ✔.\n- mysql_query verification: **attempted 7 times; all failed with `1045 Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`** — the database is unreachable in this session, so data-level verification could not be performed. This is stated explicitly rather than guessed around.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (ACADEMIC_YEAR, ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC, TERM_CODE), COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (TOTAL_UNITS, DEPARTMENT_NAME, TERM_CODE), LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL (LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY, TERM_CODE).\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** Two per-year aggregations (one for the Mathematics subject population, one for the status-'U' reserve population joined to catalog units through the term), each computing `STDDEV(TOTAL_UNITS)/AVG(TOTAL_UNITS)`, then joined on ACADEMIC_YEAR and ordered by ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC. Only the three requested columns are selected.\n\n**6c. Reasons:** *Data* — all required columns physically exist per retrieved definitions; TERM_CODE is the documented universal join key; *Semantic-network* — hint join keys list only TERM_CODE joins via ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, and column_concept decision guides route unit statistics to CCSO.TOTAL_UNITS and status filtering to LRM.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY; *Business* — dw_4701 is a same-shape precedent computing per-year AVG/STDDEV of TOTAL_UNITS over the 'U' reserve population via a term-level join.\n\n**6d. Alternatives:** joining LRM↔CCSO additionally on SUBJECT_ID (dw_1301 style) is a plausible alternative, but the hints omit that join key and dw_4701 (the closest task-shape precedent for TOTAL_UNITS statistics) uses the term-level join; the tie-breaker would be the gold SQL's join list, which the hints already indicate.\n\nFinal SQL:\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_b709c6c77bab49de9a00be17",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "submit_SQL",
            "arguments": "{\"sql\": \"WITH subject_cv AS (\\n    SELECT\\n        ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR,\\n        ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC,\\n        STDDEV(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) / AVG(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) AS cv_total_units_subjects\\n    FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ata\\n    JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso\\n        ON ata.TERM_CODE = ccso.TERM_CODE\\n    WHERE ccso.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\\n    GROUP BY ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\\n),\\nlibrary_cv AS (\\n    SELECT\\n        ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR,\\n        ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC,\\n        STDDEV(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) / AVG(ccso.TOTAL_UNITS) AS cv_total_units_library\\n    FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ata\\n    JOIN LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL lrm\\n        ON ata.TERM_CODE = lrm.TERM_CODE\\n    JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ccso\\n        ON ata.TERM_CODE = ccso.TERM_CODE\\n    WHERE lrm.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U'\\n      AND ccso.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\\n    GROUP BY ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR, ata.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\\n)\\nSELECT\\n    s.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC,\\n    s.cv_total_units_subjects,\\n    l.cv_total_units_library\\nFROM subject_cv s\\nJOIN library_cv l\\n    ON s.ACADEMIC_YEAR = l.ACADEMIC_YEAR\\nORDER BY s.ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\"}"
          }
        }
      ]
